speechtext:
Well, I suppose I shall have to be out of order myself for a moment and we shall talk about the report. I am now ready to table-as a matter of fact I did communicate to the hon. member certain reports which I had'-(1) order in council appointing members of the veterans' assistance commission; (2) order in council substituting Mr. MacNicoI for Brigadier-General Ross as a member of the commission; (3) interim report re employment of ex-service men in the maritimes, dated, November 3, 1935; (4) interim report re corps of commissionaires dated November 3, 1936;	(5)
interim report re preservation of forests in the maritimes, dated, December 10, 1936;
(6)	interim report re the establishment of a community centre, dated December 17, 1936;
(7)	second interim report re corps of commissionaires, dated December 18, 1936; (8) second interim report re employment of exservice men in the maritimes, dated January 20, 1937; (9) preliminary report of the activities of the veterans' assistance commission, dated January 21, 1937; (10) copy of letter addressed by the minister to each member of each honorary local committee; (11) order in council re a corps of commissionaires; (12) order in council re the establishment of a community centre. I have received another interim report from tile commission but am not prepared to table it at the present moment because I am asking the commission to clarify it and give me further details regarding it. I will undertake this, however, for the sake of my hon. friend and any others who are interested, that this report will be tabled in ample time for discussion in the house before parliament prorogues.
